{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:31801798 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:31801798 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"31801798","source":"MED","pmid":"31801798","pmcid":"PMC7025502","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC7025502"]},"doi":"10.1261/rna.072066.119","title":"An ancient type of MnmA protein is an iron-sulfur cluster-dependent sulfurtransferase for tRNA anticodons.","authorString":"Shigi N, Horitani M, Miyauchi K, Suzuki T, Kuroki M.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Shigi N","lastName":"Shigi","firstName":"Naoki","initials":"N","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4452-8264"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Biotechnology Research Institute for Drug Discovery, National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology (AIST), 2-4-7 Aomi, Koto-ku, Tokyo 135-0064, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Horitani M","lastName":"Horitani","firstName":"Masaki","initials":"M","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8881-0600"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Faculty of Agriculture, Department of Applied Biochemistry and Food Science, Saga University, 1 Honjo-machi, Saga 840-8502, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Miyauchi K","lastName":"Miyauchi","firstName":"Kenjyo","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biotechnology, Graduate School of Engineering, University of Tokyo, 7-3-1 Hongo, Bunkyo-ku, Tokyo 113-8656, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Suzuki T","lastName":"Suzuki","firstName":"Tsutomu","initials":"T","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9731-1731"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biotechnology, Graduate School of Engineering, University of Tokyo, 7-3-1 Hongo, Bunkyo-ku, Tokyo 113-8656, Japan."}]}},{"fullName":"Kuroki M","lastName":"Kuroki","firstName":"Misao","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Biotechnology Research Institute for Drug Discovery, National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology (AIST), 2-4-7 Aomi, Koto-ku, Tokyo 135-0064, Japan."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8881-0600"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9731-1731"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-4452-8264"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"3","volume":"26","journalIssueId":2914557,"dateOfPublication":"2020 Mar","monthOfPublication":3,"yearOfPublication":2020,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"RNA","title":"RNA (New York, N.Y.)","essn":"1469-9001","issn":"1355-8382","nlmid":"9509184","isoabbreviation":"RNA"},"printPublicationDate":"2020-03-01"},"pubYear":"2020","pageInfo":"240-250","abstractText":"Transfer RNA (tRNA) is an adaptor molecule indispensable for assigning amino acids to codons on mRNA during protein synthesis. 2-thiouridine (s<sup>2</sup>U) derivatives in the anticodons (position 34) of tRNAs for glutamate, glutamine, and lysine are post-transcriptional modifications essential for precise and efficient codon recognition in all organisms. s<sup>2</sup>U34 is introduced either by (i) bacterial MnmA/eukaryote mitochondrial Mtu1 or (ii) eukaryote cytosolic Ncs6/archaeal NcsA, and the latter enzymes possess iron-sulfur (Fe-S) cluster. Here, we report the identification of novel-type MnmA homologs containing three conserved Cys residues, which could support Fe-S cluster binding and catalysis, in a broad range of bacteria, including thermophiles, <i>Cyanobacteria</i>, <i>Mycobacteria</i>, <i>Actinomyces</i>, <i>Clostridium</i>, and <i>Helicobacter</i> Using EPR spectroscopy, we revealed that <i>Thermus thermophilus</i> MnmA (TtMnmA) contains an oxygen-sensitive [4Fe-4S]-type cluster. Efficient in vitro formation of s<sup>2</sup>U34 in tRNA<sup>Lys</sup> and tRNA<sup>Gln</sup> by holo-TtMnmA occurred only under anaerobic conditions. Mutational analysis of TtMnmA suggested that the Fe-S cluster is coordinated by the three conserved Cys residues (Cys105, Cys108, and Cys200), and is essential for its activity. Evolutionary scenarios for the sulfurtransferases, including the Fe-S cluster containing Ncs6/NcsA s<sup>2</sup>U thiouridylases and several distantly related sulfurtransferases, are proposed.","affiliation":"Biotechnology Research Institute for Drug Discovery, National Institute of Advanced Industrial Science and Technology (AIST), 2-4-7 Aomi, Koto-ku, Tokyo 135-0064, Japan.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"Grants-in-Aid for Scientific Research","grantId":"18H02412","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Takeda Science Foundation","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Precise Measurement Technology Promotion Foundation","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Sumitomo Electric Group CSR Foundation","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Grants-in-Aid for Scientific Research","grantId":"17H06955","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Grants-in-Aid for Scientific Research","grantId":"16K07311","orderIn":0},{"agency":"Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science, and Technology of Japan","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cyanobacteria","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Escherichia coli","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mycobacterium","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Sulfur","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier